diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1a55755..8ffe033 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,20 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "<string>" | null}`: one
+  page of items, ordered by `id` ascending.
+  - `limit` (optional): integer from 1 to 100, default 20.
+  - `cursor` (optional): opaque string taken from a previous response's
+    `next_cursor`. Omit it for the first page; pass it back unchanged for
+    each following page.
+  - `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page.
+  - 400 `{"error": "..."}` when `limit` is not an integer in range, or
+    when `cursor` is not a valid cursor.
+  - To read every item, request the first page, then keep requesting with
+    the returned `next_cursor` until it is `null`.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
+Example: `{"method": "GET", "path": "/items", "query": {"limit": "2"}}`
+returns items 1 and 2 with `"next_cursor": "3"`.
+
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
